{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nHiding done / closed items should not require a local view per layout: the saved views (Table / Board / Timeline) still show everything, and `is:open` / `is:closed` in a filter are ignored because the board carries no item state.\n\n## Spec\n\n1. **`projects-filter \"<expression>\"`** — a top-level node whose filter is stacked on every view's own filter, saved or local (both must match).\n2. **`is:open` / `is:closed` / `is:merged`** — the board's GraphQL items query also reads the content's `state` (and `merged` for PRs); `ProjectItem` carries it (disk cache compatible, `#[serde(default)]`), the filter evaluates it instead of reporting it as unsupported.\n3. **`x` toggle** — hides closed items (closed issues, merged / closed PRs) on top of every view; the header says `closed hidden`, the status bar's `(N filtered out)` includes them. Drafts have no state and always show. `projects-hide-closed \"on\" | \"off\"` (default `off`) sets the initial state.\n4. Docs (Config Reference en / ja, the Projects chapter, README), demo tape, fixtures re-recorded so the recorded items carry `state`.\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:39:04Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":185,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Projects: a board-wide filter and a toggle to hide closed items"}
